  message: "YOUR BLOCKER IS FIXED, AND THE NUMBER THAT WITHHELD YOU IS THE NUMBER THAT WAS\nREMOVED. 2026-09-08, measurement 0020, INV-putug shipped.\n\nThis item was built, measured and reverted in one commit because its yield\nthrough the `dispatches_to` walk defect was 3 true against 20 false -- adding it\ntook 24 situations at 66.7% correct to 47 at 40.4%. That defect is now fixed: a\n`dispatches_to` edge out of a TYPE node is no longer read as dataflow.\n\nMEASURED ON YOUR OWN CODE. Measurement 0020's harness arms pin py.py to\n`359880a105` -- THIS RULE, present in both arms -- so the numbers below are\nexactly what this item produces with and without the walk fix:\n\n  with the rule, walk defect present   183 situations, 33 class-node hops\n  with the rule, walk defect FIXED     163 situations,  0 class-node hops\n                                        22 removed / 2 added\n\nAll 22 removals crossed a class node (zero collateral) and 0 of 22 are correct.\nThe 11 class-hop flows that had an honest route were KEPT -- including\n`generate_invoice`, which really does reach `Invoice.save` through the annotated\n`build_invoice`.\n\nSO THE TRADE THAT WITHHELD THIS ITEM NO LONGER HOLDS AS MEASURED. Re-landing is\nits own PR with its own measurement, and it must re-derive the correct/useful\nsplit on the FIXED walk rather than reusing the 40.4% -- that figure was taken\nTHROUGH the defect and is not this rule's precision. The capability itself was\nnever in doubt: 61 pretix `super().save()` sites typed, 0 wrong-type on an\nindependent whole-survey read-back.\n\nThe implementation is recoverable in full from `359880a105` (`_is_super_call`,\n`_DjangoReceiverOracle.super_write_owner`, `DjangoRelationIndex.defines_in_bases`\n+ the `class_methods` map, the `_process_call` emission branch, the `super()` arm\nin `instance_class`)."  # 0b5e
