  message: "THE isbefore EDGE FROM INV-putug STAYS, DELIBERATELY, AND THIS RECORDS WHY SO IT\nIS NOT REMOVED AS STALE.\n\nINV-putug is `pending_validation`, not `satisfied` -- the walk fix is shipped and\nmeasured (0020) but has not been through the bakeoff queue. `ready` therefore\nstill holds this item back, and that is the correct behaviour rather than a\nleftover: if the fix were later found wanting, re-landing this rule now would\nrestore exactly the 3-true-against-20-false trade it was withheld for.\n\nThere is precedent for removing such an edge once its purpose is served\n(WI-gotun's 2026-09-06 entry does it and records the removal), and this is\nNOT that case yet. The condition to remove it is simple and checkable:\n**INV-putug reaching `satisfied`.** At that point this item becomes actionable\nand the edge should go.\n\nNothing else blocks it. The implementation is recoverable in full from\n`359880a105` and the capability was never in doubt (61 pretix sites, 0\nwrong-type)."  # e625
